{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789326069,"nonce":"+Ql0u4MxwU1uDtJSxkhobMILskU=","title":"Range loops with an inlined call keep the iterate/iteratorValue calls","message":"A `for (i in 0...n)` whose body has a call the MIR inliner takes is never\nturned into a counted loop. The inliner versions the loop (fast and slow\ncopies), and the range_loop pass then sees two iterate and two\niteratorValue sites on the range and declines. Every iteration pays two\ngeneric wren_call dispatches to Range natives, about 36 ns on the\nMac, in both the baseline and the LLVM tier.\n\nFound through caribou's interop benchmark (caribou-interop/benches/\ninterop.rs, fixtures/src/bench/tally.wren): its Wren-to-Wren column read\nstatic call 47 ns, method call 39, construct 119, closure call 85, against\n3.5-6.3 for Ash's Haxe-to-Haxe column; getter and setter, whose loops\nhave no inlined call, read 3.5.\n\nReproducer (Mac, tiered llvm, 200k iterations, median of 5 after 2\nwarm-ups, ns per iteration):\n\n    static add(x) { x + 1 }\n    static wrenStatic(n) { var s = 0; for (i in 0...n) s = Tally.add(s); return s }\n\nbefore: 40.9; with WLIFT_DISABLE_LOOP_VERSIONING=1: 4.2.\n\nFix: inline_known runs RangeLoop on the compile clone before\ninline_known_calls, so the loop is counted when it is versioned. After:\nstatic call 3.9, method call 5.8, construct 7.0 on the same short run;\nsteady state once the LLVM tier lands: static 1.0, construct 4.1.","files":null}]}